      "text": [
        "811 - وَ كَتَبَ إِلَيْهِ: فِي اَلرَّجُلِ يَجْعَلُ فِي جُبَّتِهِ بَدَلَ اَلْقُطْنِ قَزّاً هَلْ يُصَلِّي فِيهِ فَكَتَبَ «نَعَمْ لاَ بَأْسَ بِهِ.\""
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.811 - He (Ibrahim ibn Mahziyar) wrote to Imam Abu Muhammad al-Hasan (as) asking about a man who replaces cotton in his cloak with qazz (a type of silk):\n\"Can he pray in it?\"\nImam (as) replied: \"Yes, there is no problem with it.\""
        ]
      }
